# a uniscript code point `\:U+12C00` `\:u+12C00` `\:U12C00` `\:0x12C00` is its one character, in either quote; a known
# name wins, a bare `\:12C00` is no code point and stays as written, a surrogate or a number past U+10FFFF is refused
# (user 2026-11-15; wiki uniscript.md)

# the four marks, in double and single quotes
'"\\:U+12C00"'	'𒰀'
'"\\:u+12C00"'	'𒰀'
'"\\:U12C00"'	'𒰀'
'"\\:0x12C00"'	'𒰀'
'\'\\:U+12C00\''	'𒰀'
'\'\\:u+12C00\''	'𒰀'
'\'\\:U12C00\''	'𒰀'
'\'\\:0x12C00\''	'𒰀'
'#"\\:U+1F600"'	1
'"caf\\:U+e9 \\:0x41"'	'café A'
'"\\:u12C00" == "\\u{12C00}"'	1

# names stay names, now in single quotes too
'"\\:alpha"'	'α'
'\'\\:alpha\''	'α'
'"\\:Ua"'	'Ⲩ'

# a bare hex number is no code point, nor is a word after the mark
'"\\:12C00"'	'\\:12C00'
'\'\\:12C00\''	'\\:12C00'
'"\\:U12C00x"'	'\\:U12C00x'

# beyond Unicode or a surrogate is refused
'"\\:U+110000"'	error	invalid code point
'"\\:0xD800"'	error	invalid code point
